  "system": {
    "role": "Qliphothic Ambusher (Satariel — Lesser)",
    "tier": 1,
    "factionId": "",
    "notes": "<p>Spider legs, a gaunt shadow-torso, too many white eyes. Veil-Spinners weave webs of pure deceit — illusory oases, familiar pathways that end in cliffs — and feed on the exact moment their prey realizes the beautiful thing was a lie. Patient hunters, embodying the Qliphah's principle: hide the truth behind a pleasing or terrifying face.</p><p><strong>Qliphah:</strong> Satariel, the Veils — the Hull of Binah. Understanding inverted into concealment.</p><p><em>Mal's note: 'Rule of thumb: in the Wastes, anything that looks like exactly what you needed to see is a mouth.'</em></p>",
